":"https://api.github.com/users/davidzchen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2016-02-25T09:17:57Z","updated_at":"2016-02-29T22:15:27Z","closed_at":"2016-02-29T22:15:27Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I have a `WORKSPACE` file which contains the following:\n\n```\nnew_git_repository(\n    name = \"boringssl\",\n    remote = \"https://boringssl.googlesource.com/boringssl\",\n    commit = \"e412bbd9a15d812666291e38e194b71da6a2a062\",\n    build_file = \"BUILD.boringssl\",\n)\nload(\"@bazel_tools//tools/build_rules/go:def.bzl\", \"go_repositories\")\ngo_repositories()\n```\n\nwhere `BUILD.boringssl` contains\n\n```\nload(\"@bazel_tools//tools/build_rules/go:def.bzl\", \"go_prefix\")\nload(\"@bazel_tools//tools/build_rules/go:def.bzl\", \"go_binary\")\ngo_prefix('boringssl')\n[...]\ngo_binary(\n    name = \"err_data_generate\",\n    srcs = [\"crypto/err/err_data_generate.go\"],\n)\n```\n\nThen `bazel build @boringssl//:err_data_generate` works as expected on Mac OS X, but on Linux, it fails with the following error:\n\n```\nERROR: .../BUILD:915:1: every rule of type go_binary implicitly depends upon the target '@//tools/build_rules/go/toolchain:toolchain', but this target could not be found because of: no such package '@//tools/build_rules/go/toolchain': BUILD file not found on package path.\n```\n\nThen I tried re-compiling Bazel after editing https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/blob/6beaebdfa7ea3d0bcfd58511dbf6f588b206914d/tools/build_rules/go/def.bzl#L322-L327 to replace `@//tools` with `@bazel_tools//tools`, and that version seems to work fine.\n\nIs this change correct to make? I don't understand the difference between using `//tools`, `@//tools`, and `@bazel_tools//tools`, and also why it initially worked on OS X but not on Linux.\n","closed_by":{"login":"kchodorow","id":17042,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MDQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17042?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow","html_url":"https://github.com/kchodorow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kchodorow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/976/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/976/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}